<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sancho II of Pamplona</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 994</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> · Also known as Sancho Garcés II, Sancho Abarca</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sancho II Garcés, called Abarca, was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pamplona">Pamplona</a> from 970 to 994, son of García Sánchez I. Following his father's will, he gave the Rioja lands around Viguera to his brother Ramiro with the title of king. Pressed by the raids of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almanzor">Almanzor</a>, he became a tributary of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">Caliphate</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cordoba">Córdoba</a> and gave a daughter in marriage to Almanzor; she became the mother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abd-al-rahman-sanchuelo">Abd al-Rahman Sanchuelo</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sancho-ii-of-pamplona.jpg" alt="Sancho II of Pamplona" width="320" height="480" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sancho2Navarra.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
